operator adoption, and tracking issues are filed in the COO Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects.\n5. The guideline records the resolved decision on optional fields beyond name/namespace/resourceKind.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 (P1): convention documented as a contribution guideline and published for external operator adoption\n\n**ai-signals files**: one per epic, markdown table Signal/Value/Rationale.\n\nNow write everything. Use Write tool for bodies, then frontmatter.py set for FM, then batch-read, validate, then set decompose_complete.\n\nFor frontmatter set with ai_signals nested keys: `ai_signals.change_specificity=1` etc. as in the example.\n\nEpic files:\n\nE001: epic_id=RHAISTRAT-8010-E001, title=\"Convert rhods-operator manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured fields\", parent_strat=RHAISTRAT-8010, component=\"AI Core Platform\", team=\"ODH Operator team\", type=Implementation, priority=P0, dependencies=\"\" (none — root). Set dependencies empty? Just omit (default []). \n\nE002: same, P0, no dependencies.\n\nE003: P1, dependencies=\"RHAISTRAT-8010-E001,RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\".\n\nE004: P1, implementation_type=docs-authoring, dependencies=\"RHAISTRAT-8010-E001,RHAISTRAT-8010-E002,RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\".\n\nTitles with spaces — quote them in shell.\n\nLet me now write all files. First the decomposition summary body.\n\nAlso: does the validator check summary for overage acknowledgment regex and require \"re-split trigger\"? My health warning includes \"**Re-split trigger**:\" — good, and the overage ack regex looks for \"above ... guideline\" phrasing — mine says \"above the ~2-week guideline\". The regex: `\\b(?:above|...)\\s*[^.\\n]{0,80}?\\b(?:guideline|2-week|...)` — \"above the ~2-week guideline\" matches \"above\" then within 80 chars \"guideline\". Good. And it must find a re-split trigger somewhere — \"Re-split trigger:\" present. Good.\n\nBundled check: summary acknowledges HLR-7 bundled into P0 epic → matrix row must carry `