{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8ac4b841-2564-4ff3-b33a-5addb4b5ccc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8836391ef4da42a3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-tqi78i_c/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Convert rhods-operator manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured fields\n\n## Description\n\nConverts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and standardizes structured field names across all reconciliation error log paths in the manager binary of the rhods-operator: the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers, the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), and the 15 action files across 4 tiers. Resource name and namespace move out of message strings into structured `name`/`namespace` fields; `resourceKind` is added as a structured field to all controllers; DSCI's non-standard keys (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) migrate to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager-binary reconciliation error paths (grep/static analysis), producing a coverage checklist of call sites that embed resource identity in message text — the strategy's 75% figure is an estimate to be confirmed by this audit\n- For each embedding call site, extract the resource identity from the message string and convert it to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), keeping message text compatible with existing log ingestion\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in: the 5 service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSC controller and the 8 component controllers, and the DSCI controller\n- Migrate DSCI structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`\n- Cover all 15 action files across the 4 tiers: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`)\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): `namespace` omitted or set to empty string, never a spurious value\n- Unit tests asserting structured field presence and correctness via test logger output\n- Backwards-compatibility validation per the strategy's NFR: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, and a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack configured to verify ingestion of both formats; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update any text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Static analysis of the manager binary flags no remaining `log.Error` calls with resource name/namespace embedded in message text; every affected call site uses structured `name`/`namespace` key-value pairs.\n2. A grep of the codebase confirms no references to the old DSCI field names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) remain, and a unit test asserts DSCI error logs contain `name` and `namespace` with correct values.\n3. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct value for each of the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n4. Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values across all 15 action files in all 4 tiers.\n5. Unit tests assert module controller error logs (all 8 module handlers) include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`.\n6. Unit tests assert DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n7. A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value (namespace omitted or set to empty string).\n8. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes; a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack shows logs ingested correctly, and text-based alert rules relying on changed message strings are identified with updates coordinated with SRE/Support.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): message-embedded resource identity converted to structured key-value pairs — manager binary paths\n- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names to camelCase convention\n- HLR-3 (P0): service controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`\n- HLR-4 (P0): action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers\n- HLR-6 (P0): module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers)\n- HLR-7 (P1, bundled): DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` — bundled with the P0 conversion because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites in the same controller files as the P0 name/namespace work; a split would double-touch the same files and duplicate the call-site audit\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65383,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e598d1e70fa3cc5","agent_id":"abffdc8aa7ff76948","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"bd2f49c1-ee6b-4bf4-882f-fea40177134b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:41:38.049Z","subagent_type":"c