{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8ac4b841-2564-4ff3-b33a-5addb4b5ccc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bff8da140646cd65","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-tqi78i_c/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Convert cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs to structured fields\n\n## Description\n\nApplies the structured-logging conversion to the cloudmanager binary of the rhods-operator, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern and already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit `log.Error()` call sites in the three cloudmanager controller reconciliation error paths\n- Convert call sites that embed resource name or namespace in message strings to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`)\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all three controllers' reconciliation error logs (`name`/`namespace` are already provided by the shared reconciler)\n- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output\n- Before/after log output comparison covering cloud log consumers (e.g., CloudWatch) per the strategy's backwards-compatibility NFR\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Static analysis flags no remaining `log.Error` calls in cloudmanager reconciliation error paths with resource identity embedded in message text.\n2. Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values in test logger output for all three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n3. A before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Release timing (same release as the manager-binary work vs. a subsequent release) is an open PM scheduling question; this work is independently schedulable and deferrable, since cloudmanager is only deployed on non-OpenShift Kubernetes and its impact scope is narrower. If deferred, the repository-wide CI lint enforcement is scoped to manager-binary paths until this conversion ships.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): message-embedded resource identity converted to structured key-value pairs — cloudmanager binary paths\n- HLR-5 (P0): cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65383,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e598d1e70fa3cc5","agent_id":"abffdc8aa7ff76948","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"61fc2832-ed36-451a-83ed-94e248d6b91d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:41:44.377Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 into epics"}
