{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8ac4b841-2564-4ff3-b33a-5addb4b5ccc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2dc81984293129a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-tqi78i_c/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# CI lint enforcement for structured reconciliation log fields\n\n## Description\n\nAdds a CI lint/static-analysis rule to the rhods-operator repository that durably enforces the structured logging convention: it flags any `log.Error` call in reconciliation error paths that embeds resource name or namespace in the message text or omits the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`). This turns the strategy's acceptance measurement (\"CI lint rule or static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text\") into a permanent regression gate covering new controller development.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement a lint/static-analysis check that detects `log.Error` calls embedding resource identity in message text or missing the required structured fields in reconciliation error paths, applicable across both the manager and cloudmanager binaries of the repository\n- Wire the check into the repository's CI so it gates new changes\n- The rule lands after the manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary conversions are complete so that it passes on the converted codebase; if the cloudmanager conversion is deferred to a subsequent release per the open scheduling question, the rule is scoped to manager-binary paths until that conversion ships\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. The CI lint rule runs in the repository's CI pipeline and flags `log.Error` calls with resource name/namespace embedded in message text.\n2. The rule passes on the fully converted codebase (zero violations across the manager and cloudmanager binaries).\n3. A deliberately introduced violation on a test branch is flagged by the rule, demonstrating the gate catches regressions.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, enforcement aspect): provides the durable CI lint enforcement cited by HLR-1's \"measured by\" clause; the P0 conversion itself is carried by the manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary conversion work\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65383,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e598d1e70fa3cc5","agent_id":"abffdc8aa7ff76948","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"de71e836-0a70-4350-902a-e7cbffbc4baf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:41:48.627Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 into epics"}
