he required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n2. The guideline includes before/after code examples for the message-embedded-identity conversion and a DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples.\n3. The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging behavior — a reviewer confirms the documented examples and field names match the shipped code.\n4. The convention is published for external operator adoption, and tracking issues are filed in the COO Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects.\n5. The guideline records the resolved decision on optional fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind`.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- COO team adoption is voluntary and best-effort per platform policy; filing tracking issues is in scope, but their prioritization is outside this strategy's control.\n- The strategy's Documentation Support prerequisite is pending human review; the technical review acceptance criterion covers accuracy against the implementation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 (P1): convention documented as a contribution guideline for new controller development and published for external operator adoption\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65383,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e598d1e70fa3cc5","agent_id":"abffdc8aa7ff76948","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"4ff20e61-9fa1-4d34-8b4f-ddc7ce04450b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:41:55.451Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 into epics"}
