{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c2f7ee279ee46f3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Convert rhods-operator manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured\n4\t  fields\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Convert rhods-operator manager binary reconciliation error logs to structured fields\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConverts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and standardizes structured field names across all reconciliation error log paths in the manager binary of the rhods-operator: the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers, the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), and the 15 action files across 4 tiers. Resource name and namespace move out of message strings into structured `name`/`namespace` fields; `resourceKind` is added as a structured field to all controllers; DSCI's non-standard keys (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) migrate to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in manager-binary reconciliation error paths (grep/static analysis), producing a coverage checklist of call sites that embed resource identity in message text — the strategy's 75% figure is an estimate to be confirmed by this audit\n39\t- For each embedding call site, extract the resource identity from the message string and convert it to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), keeping message text compatible with existing log ingestion\n40\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in: the 5 service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSC controller and the 8 component controllers, and the DSCI controller\n41\t- Migrate DSCI structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`\n42\t- Cover all 15 action files across the 4 tiers: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`)\n43\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): `namespace` omitted or set to empty string, never a spurious value\n44\t- Unit tests asserting structured field presence and correctness via test logger output\n45\t- Backwards-compatibility validation per the strategy's NFR: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, and a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack configured to verify ingestion of both formats; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update any text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t1. Static analysis of the manager binary flags no remaining `log.Error` calls with resource name/namespace embedded in message text; every affected call site uses structured `name`/`namespace` key-value pairs.\n50\t2. A grep of the codebase confirms no references to the old DSCI field names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) remain, and a unit test asserts DSCI error logs contain `name` and `namespace` with correct values.\n51\t3. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct value for each of the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n52\t4. Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values across all 15 action files in all 4 tiers.\n53\t5. Unit tests assert module controller error logs (all 8 module handlers) include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`.\n54\t6. Unit tests assert DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n55\t7. A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value (namespace omitted or set to empty string).\n56\t8. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes; a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack shows logs ingested correctly, and text-based alert rules relying on changed message strings are identified with updates coordinated with SRE/Support.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-1 (P0): message-embedded resource identity converted to structured key-value pairs — manager binary paths\n61\t- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names to camelCase convention\n62\t- HLR-3 (P0): service controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`\n63\t- HLR-4 (P0): action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers\n64\t- HLR-6 (P0): module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers)\n65\t- HLR-7 (P1, bundled): DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` — bundled with the P0 conversion because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites in the same controller files as the P0 name/namespace work; a split would double-touch the same files and duplicate the call-site audit\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97a05a4ae9ca92f5","agent_id":"abebec9c24d08fcdf","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"d9a37d49-6d7b-4db8-884e-7456ad6df7dc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:47.938Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c2f7ee279ee46f3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
