{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a372826e52b7955","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Convert cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs to structured fields\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Convert cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs to structured fields\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tApplies the structured-logging conversion to the cloudmanager binary of the rhods-operator, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern and already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit `log.Error()` call sites in the three cloudmanager controller reconciliation error paths\n38\t- Convert call sites that embed resource name or namespace in message strings to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`)\n39\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all three controllers' reconciliation error logs (`name`/`namespace` are already provided by the shared reconciler)\n40\t- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output\n41\t- Before/after log output comparison covering cloud log consumers (e.g., CloudWatch) per the strategy's backwards-compatibility NFR\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t1. Static analysis flags no remaining `log.Error` calls in cloudmanager reconciliation error paths with resource identity embedded in message text.\n46\t2. Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values in test logger output for all three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n47\t3. A before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n48\t\n49\t## Risks / Notes\n50\t\n51\t- Release timing (same release as the manager-binary work vs. a subsequent release) is an open PM scheduling question; this work is independently schedulable and deferrable, since cloudmanager is only deployed on non-OpenShift Kubernetes and its impact scope is narrower. If deferred, the repository-wide CI lint enforcement is scoped to manager-binary paths until this conversion ships.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-1 (P0): message-embedded resource identity converted to structured key-value pairs — cloudmanager binary paths\n56\t- HLR-5 (P0): cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97a05a4ae9ca92f5","agent_id":"abebec9c24d08fcdf","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"dd7e7734-9d12-4493-afdf-5cc7cab8c0de","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:48.675Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a372826e52b7955","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
