{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be4bbebb3a6f3572","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: CI lint enforcement for structured reconciliation log fields\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# CI lint enforcement for structured reconciliation log fields\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAdds a CI lint/static-analysis rule to the rhods-operator repository that durably enforces the structured logging convention: it flags any `log.Error` call in reconciliation error paths that embeds resource name or namespace in the message text or omits the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`). This turns the strategy's acceptance measurement (\"CI lint rule or static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text\") into a permanent regression gate covering new controller development.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Implement a lint/static-analysis check that detects `log.Error` calls embedding resource identity in message text or missing the required structured fields in reconciliation error paths, applicable across both the manager and cloudmanager binaries of the repository\n40\t- Wire the check into the repository's CI so it gates new changes\n41\t- The rule lands after the manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary conversions are complete so that it passes on the converted codebase; if the cloudmanager conversion is deferred to a subsequent release per the open scheduling question, the rule is scoped to manager-binary paths until that conversion ships\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t1. The CI lint rule runs in the repository's CI pipeline and flags `log.Error` calls with resource name/namespace embedded in message text.\n46\t2. The rule passes on the fully converted codebase (zero violations across the manager and cloudmanager binaries).\n47\t3. A deliberately introduced violation on a test branch is flagged by the rule, demonstrating the gate catches regressions.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (P0, enforcement aspect): provides the durable CI lint enforcement cited by HLR-1's \"measured by\" clause; the P0 conversion itself is carried by the manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary conversion work\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97a05a4ae9ca92f5","agent_id":"abebec9c24d08fcdf","session_id":"cd28af09-5096-4047-9ddc-e7a6fc26f678","uuid":"868112d0-e29c-40b4-84ee-f4e5965a91cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:51.746Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be4bbebb3a6f3572","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
