 No konflux chain applies. Soft-AC scan: E001 AC8's dev-cluster validation is work the epic performs (deploy test build, trigger errors, verify ingestion), not an externally-granted availability precondition — correctly an AC, not a risk note; the externally-controlled items (COO adoption, pending process gates, release timing) are correctly placed in Risks/Notes and Health Warnings. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic mentions use descriptive names (\"the manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary conversions\", \"the repository-wide CI lint enforcement\").\n35\t\n36\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n37\tEvery strategy acceptance criterion maps to an epic AC: conversion (E001 AC1, E002 AC1), DSCI migration (E001 AC2), service-controller resourceKind (E001 AC3), 15 action files across 4 tiers (E001 AC4), cloudmanager (E002 AC2), cluster-scoped resources (E001 AC7), documented convention (E004 AC1/AC2). The SME overrides are faithfully applied (15 action files / 4 tiers, module-controller tier added as HLR-6, the answered \"~16 files\" question correctly not turned into an Investigation). The backwards-compatibility NFR is carried into both conversion epics; the performance NFR requires no verification per the strategy itself. Strategy-level context is not dropped: all four risks map to epic-level mitigations (coverage checklist + lint gate, dev-cluster validation, E004 publication/tracking issues, migration guide + release notes), and all four open questions are dispositioned in the summary. The strategy's \"to be created\" design-doc content (three-problem diagnosis, before/after examples, DSCI migration guide) is fully covered by E004's scope. External COO work is correctly excluded per platform policy overlay 0008 and documented in Health Warnings and Tiered Delivery. Docs-authoring epic present and docs-last (Rule 11), confirmed by the validator.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6e8a294cf1eae2d","agent_id":"a950e340a5677034d","sess